ommits/24be88f4116135d34397734b3bd4e9c34832dac1","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6507750?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ctlaltdieliet/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ctlaltdieliet/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ctlaltdieliet/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ctlaltdieliet/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ctlaltdieliet","id":6507750,"login":"ctlaltdieliet","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY1MDc3NTA=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ctlaltdieliet/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ctlaltdieliet/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ctlaltdieliet/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ctlaltdieliet/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ctlaltdieliet/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ctlaltdieliet","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/manish-gitx/sst-mattermost/commit/24be88f4116135d34397734b3bd4e9c34832dac1","node_id":"C_kwDOOd4PsNoAKDI0YmU4OGY0MTE2MTM1ZDM0Mzk3NzM0YjNiZDRlOWMzNDgzMmRhYzE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/manish-gitx/sst-mattermost/commit/d8dbb6cc22156d5257e4fb5a54ba6d0afd11636c","sha":"d8dbb6cc22156d5257e4fb5a54ba6d0afd11636c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/manish-gitx/sst-mattermost/commits/d8dbb6cc22156d5257e4fb5a54ba6d0afd11636c"}],"sha":"24be88f4116135d34397734b3bd4e9c34832dac1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/manish-gitx/sst-mattermost/commits/24be88f4116135d34397734b3bd4e9c34832dac1"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1774000?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/agnivade/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/agnivade/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/agnivade/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/agnivade/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/agnivade","id":1774000,"login":"agnivade","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NzQwMDA=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/agnivade/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/agnivade/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/agnivade/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/agnivade/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/agnivade/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/agnivade","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/manish-gitx/sst-mattermost/commits/d8dbb6cc22156d5257e4fb5a54ba6d0afd11636c/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2025-04-22T05:13:13Z","email":"agnivade@yahoo.co.in","name":"Agniva De Sarker"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2025-04-22T05:13:13Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"MM-56548: [AI assisted]Add support for incremental thread loading using UpdateAt timestamp (#30486)\n\nEvery time we load the RHS, we used to load the FULL thread always. Although\nthe actual ThreadViewer React component is virtualized, and the server side\nAPI call is paginated, we still went through all the pages, to get the full\nthread and passed it on to the ThreadViewer. This would be for first loads,\nand subsequent loads of the same thread.\n\nThis was a bug originally, but then it was a necessity after we applied websocket event scope because\nnow we won''t get emoji reactions of a thread if the user is not on the thread.\n\nTo fix that, we enhance the thread loading functionality by adding support for fetching\nthread updates based on the UpdateAt timestamp. Now, for subsequent loads,\nwe only get the changed posts in a thread. The implementation:\n\n- Adds new API parameters: fromUpdateAt and updatesOnly to the GetPostThread endpoint\n- Updates database queries to support sorting and filtering by UpdateAt\n- Implements thread state management to track the last update timestamp\n- Adds client-side support to use incremental loading for improved performance\n- Ensures proper validation for parameter combinations and error handling\n\nThis change enables more efficient thread loading, particularly for long threads\nwith frequent updates, by only fetching posts that have been updated since the\nlast view.\n\nCaveats: For delta updates, the SQL query won''t use the best index possible\nbecause we have an index for (CreateAt, Id), but no index for (UpdateAt, Id).\nHowever, from my tests, it is not as bad as it looks:\n\n```\n[loadtest] # EXPLAIN (ANALYZE, BUFFERS) SELECT * FROM Posts WHERE Posts.DeleteAt = 0 AND Posts.RootId = ''qbr5gctu9iyg8c36hpcq6f3w8e'' AND Posts.UpdateAt > 1623445795824 ORDER BY UpdateAt ASC, Id ASC LIMIT 61;\n                                                                   QUERY PLAN\n-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n Limit  (cost=8.31..8.31 rows=1 width=216) (actual time=0.047..0.049 rows=0 loops=1)\n   Buffers: shared hit=2\n   ->  Sort  (cost=8.31..8.31 rows=1 width=216) (actual time=0.044..0.045 rows=0 loops=1)\n         Sort Key: updateat, id\n         Sort Method: quicksort  Memory: 25kB\n         Buffers: shared hit=2\n         ->  Index Scan using idx_posts_root_id_delete_at on posts  (cost=0.28..8.30 rows=1 width=216) (actual time=0.031..0.032 rows=0 loops=1)\n               Index Cond: (((rootid)::text = ''qbr5gctu9iyg8c36hpcq6f3w8e''::text) AND (deleteat = 0))\n               Filter: (updateat > ''1623445795824''::bigint)\n               Buffers: shared hit=2\n Planning:\n   Buffers: shared hit=3\n Planning Time: 0.508 ms\n Execution Time: 0.106 ms\n(14 rows)\n```\n\nWe still get an index scan with index cond. Although there''s a filter element, but atleast we get the whole thread with the index.\nMy thinking is that while the whole thread might be large, but after that, updates on a thread should be incremental.\nTherefore, we should be okay without adding yet another index on the posts table.\n\nThis is just the first step in what could be potentially improved further.\n\n1. We shouldn''t even be loading the full thread always. But rather let the virtualized viewer\nload more posts on demand.\n2. If a post has been just reacted to, then we need not send the whole post down, but just the\nreaction. This further saves bandwidth.\n\nhttps://mattermost.atlassian.net/browse/MM-56548\n\nTBD: Add load-test coverage to update the thread loading code\n\n```release-note\nNONE\n```\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Mattermost Build <build@mattermost.com>","tree":{"sha":"29f41267c38f988c65698e4a9e461706795b17c7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/manish-gitx/sst-mattermost/git/trees/29f41267c38f988c65698e4a9e461706795b17c7"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/manish-gitx/sst-mattermost/git/commits/d8dbb6cc22156d5257e4fb5a54ba6d0afd11636c","verification":{"payload":"tree 29f41267c38f988c65698e4a9e461706795b17c7\nparent d631974e882c1c1442b151247192f9bbb2161268\nauthor Agniva De Sarker <agnivade@yahoo.co.in> 1745298793 +0530\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1745298793 +0530\n\nMM-56548: [AI assisted]Add support for incremental thread loading using UpdateAt timestamp (#30486)\n\nEvery time we load the RHS, we used to load the FULL thread always. Although\nthe actual ThreadViewer React component is virtualized, and the server side\nAPI call is paginated, we still went through all the pages, to get the full\nthread and passed it on to the ThreadViewer. This would be for first loads,\nand subsequent loads of the same thread.\n\nThis was a bug originally, but then it was a necessity after we applied websocket event scope because\nnow we won''t get emoji reactions of a thread if the user is not on the thread.\n\nTo fix that, we enhance the thread loading functionality by adding support for fetching\nthread updates based on the UpdateAt timestamp. Now, for subsequent loads,\nwe only get the changed posts in a thread. The implementation:\n\n- Adds new API parameters: fromUpdateAt and updatesOnly to the GetPostThread endpoint\n- Updates database queries to support sorting and filtering by UpdateAt\n- Implements thread state management to track the last update timestamp\n- Adds client-side support to use incremental loading for improved performance\n- Ensures proper validation for parameter combinations and error handling\n\nThis change enables more efficient thread loading, particularly for long threads\nwith frequent updates, by only fetching posts that have been updated since the\nlast view.\n\nCaveats: For delta updates, the SQL query won''t use the best index possible\nbecause we have an index for (CreateAt, Id), but no index for (UpdateAt, Id).\nHowever, from my tests, it is not as bad as it looks:\n\n```\n[loadtest] # EXPLAIN (ANALYZE, BUFFERS) SELECT * FROM Posts WHERE Posts.DeleteAt = 0 AND Posts.RootId = ''qbr5gctu9iyg8c36hpcq6f3w8e'' AND Posts.UpdateAt > 1623445795824 ORDER BY UpdateAt ASC, Id ASC LIMIT 61;\n                                                                   QUERY PLAN\n-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n Limit  (cost=8.31..8.31 rows=1 width=216) (actual time=0.047..0.049 rows=0 loops=1)\n   Buffers: shared hit=2\n   ->  Sort  (cost=8.31..8.31 rows=1 width=216) (actual time=0.044..0.045 rows=0 loops=1)\n         Sort Key: updateat, id\n         Sort Method: quicksort  Memory: 25kB\n         Buffers: shared hit=2\n         ->  Index Scan using idx_posts_root_id_delete_at on posts  (cost=0.28..8.30 rows=1 width=216) (actual time=0.031..0.032 rows=0 loops=1)\n               Index Cond: (((rootid)::text = ''qbr5gctu9iyg8c36hpcq6f3w8e''::text) AND (deleteat = 0))\n               Filter: (updateat > ''1623445795824''::bigint)\n               Buffers: shared hit=2\n Planning:\n   Buffers: shared hit=3\n Planning Time: 0.508 ms\n Execution Time: 0.106 ms\n(14 rows)\n```\n\nWe still get an index scan with index cond. Although there''s a filter element, but atleast we get the whole thread with the index.\nMy thinking is that while the whole thread might be large, but after that, updates on a thread should be incremental.\nTherefore, we should be okay without adding yet another index on the posts table.\n\nThis is just the first step in what could be potentially improved further.\n\n1. We shouldn''t even be loading the full thread always. But rather let the virtualized viewer\nload more posts on demand.\n2. If a post has been just reacted to, then we need not send the whole post down, but just the\nreaction. This further saves bandwidth.\n\nhttps://mattermost.atlassian.net/browse/MM-56548\n\nTBD: Add load-test coverage to update the thread loading code\n\n```release-note\nNONE\n```\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Mattermost Build <build@mattermost.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJoByVpCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAVFgQAGQqlGcYSuy6YfcZCPg7T1BU\n6mie+h6sjpHNrq82MlWLYkFVOeLIrlKFAsZO1FBSyUxGfKg03rHheIG5GJkpn46O\nNtsteg+KeJuzuBwkRTKyZKjEJvgZzfgJrE1C6T7uzbT/kThxS5U/NY8a0fFnhUxS\n9UFd0PRlw7279FV2MMhKVexHjeBHNlJCaAkiIzA3XGJMCdiYYFB6SSHMMe/akzlj\nRfL8l1MnpwRncuuWjWsJTwLOQgLmAym9jijvbZyCNEKdhCqQLhud7Kn+L6ohh3XN\nXHQS8B5u322R5lZfz7ozykbD/L5bOn5vASdGn25VCjxdTSQbV5uz6td+ipjpIOZ6\nt8DQyNO5jjLGHnUxYQjsA8IxowSqraIGEowkr+qVOJS6hyFXZHDZz58CneEVIyvh\n/oiDN4Tar4dt9ibDaeHe+MfIAZrHuthp8MG0ikayFtrmboEsoqJVVB2txMDue5vv\nTTrGnB1w1+6vqHPiKLrkAsEqpdTeP2pdZp772I2+4AHBCcfAkEBBL1G6+NsGVE1q\ncfxugzGe0FPkSDkQqcc8EFVKdHIhAgbFFzx8w+kcxitHVbRRYA12qUGp7VGS4zNQ\n1ERWgPg53bQmzgBuh01XjVHQAb5cmkToZmfttWbXiNpSHu739VJKptqs/C+OMCIG\n2ZfWo4NKvv3FmVPmoDj3\n=crLu\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE---